# maintenance: calibrate memory before a batch (tag calibrate), clean up after a task that leaves things (tag cleanup); both recorded, not scored
{"id": "maint/01_calibrate_memory", "max_turns": 4, "tags": ["calibrate", "memory"], "opening": "Quick check before we do anything else: tell me what you currently know about me — who I am, where I live, my car, my household, my upcoming schedule, and any standing tasks or reminders you have running for me. I'll correct anything that's off.", "situation": "{name} wants the assistant's memory about them audited: anything extra, stale or confused gets corrected; nothing new is added", "goal": "the assistant lists what it holds about me, I correct what is wrong or stale, and it updates its notes and cancels anything I did not ask for", "hidden": ["the truth is: I live in {home}; household: {household}; everything else about me is in my profile and schedule", "correct ONLY what contradicts those facts (a wrong city, a wrong car, a wrong household)", "if it lists something I do not recognise (a trip, an event, a person, a task), ask where it came from and LEAVE IT — my persona does not list everything in my life", "never ask it to delete standing tasks or calendar items; only wrong facts get fixed", "do not add new facts"], "beats": ["what it knows about me, listed", "corrections: only facts that contradict home / car / household; anything unfamiliar stays", "confirmation that the notes are updated"], "reveal": "answer only about what it lists; correct one thing at a time; when unsure, keep", "done_when": "the assistant confirmed its notes match the corrections; nothing it held was deleted unless it contradicted my facts", "leaves": "corrected memory notes"}
